## Code layout

```text
apps/
  api/                 Go or Rust API, its Dockerfile, tests, and docs
  web/                 Next.js App Router app, BFF, and TanStack Query hooks
.github/workflows/     root CI aggregation (ci feature only)
CONTEXT-MAP.md         API/web/workspace context boundary and runtime flow
CONTEXT.md             cross-app engineering rules
Makefile               one entry point for install, dev, test, and CI
compose.yaml           root full-stack Compose file (docker feature)
```

Read `apps/api/README.md` and `apps/web/README.md` for each app's module map.
Read `CONTEXT-MAP.md` before changing authentication or cross-app wiring.
Desktop offline sync is documented in `docs/SYNC.md`, `docs/CONFLICTS.md`, and
`docs/IDEMPOTENCY.md`.

<!-- smokeforge:anchor desktop-readme -->

## First run

```bash
make install
make api-dev   # API on http://localhost:8080
make web-dev   # web on http://localhost:3000
```

Docker:

```bash
make docker-up
```

The web app talks to the API through its same-origin BFF. Browser code never
receives the API access or refresh token. Set `API_URL` for the Next.js server
and `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` for the browser origin. See
[CONTEXT-MAP.md](CONTEXT-MAP.md) before changing authentication or data flow.

